{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772733587,"nonce":"zn2tocjLnSQMLXh//IezR1B8WZY=","title":"node-pty spawn-helper missing execute bit after npm install","message":"node_modules/node-pty/prebuilds/darwin-arm64/spawn-helper is installed with permissions 644 (not executable) by npm. node-pty's own postinstall script only fixes build/Release/spawn-helper, not the prebuild variants. \n\nResult: every PTY spawn fails immediately with \"posix_spawnp failed.\" — shell/claude/codex console sessions never reach running state, WebSocket is rejected by addWsClient, and the UI shows \"Disconnected\" immediately on every new session.\n\nThis was the root cause of the persistent disconnect bug in the console tab.\n\nFix options:\n1. Add a postinstall script to Mandible's package.json that chmod +x any spawn-helper found in node-pty prebuilds/\n2. Add a startup check in src/index.ts that verifies and fixes spawn-helper permissions on launch\n3. Document in CLAUDE.md and README that chmod +x node_modules/node-pty/prebuilds/*/spawn-helper is required after npm install\n\nShort-term: chmod +x was applied manually. This will be lost after the next npm install.","files":null}]}